  user_input {
    user_response: "just after the first hero section replace that image with the image Use my generated macro skin photograph as the main visual. Create an elegant two-column layout:\n\nLeft: Large, edge-to-edge macro photograph showing natural skin texture, pores and facial details.\n\nRight: Warm ivory/beige background with refined typography and generous whitespace.\n\nText:\n\nEyebrow: THE ART OF SKINCARE\n\nHeading: Beauty begins with care.\n\nDescription: Discover personalised skincare experiences designed to bring out your natural beauty.\n\nCTA: EXPLORE TREATMENTS \342\206\227\n\nUse elegant serif typography for the heading, minimal sans-serif for supporting text, and muted earthy colours.\n\nAdd a sophisticated image reveal on scroll, subtle parallax movement and smooth text entrance animations.\n\nOn mobile, stack the image above the text.\n\nThe overall result should feel like an expensive international skincare brand editorial, inspired by Odyss\303\251e. Avoid generic cards, excessive decorations and unnecessary visual effects. provided\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nMedia attachment: User sent attachment: /assets/aistudio/Generated_Image_November_17__2026_-_4_59PM_6977a387.jpg (saved in workspace at /public/assets/aistudio/Generated_Image_November_17__2026_-_4_59PM_6977a387.jpg). Read it with view_file at that path; in shell commands, which run from the workspace root, use the relative path public/assets/aistudio/Generated_Image_November_17__2026_-_4_59PM_6977a387.jpg. When displaying or embedding this asset in code, reference this local file path directly. Only invoke image generation tools if the user explicitly requests creating or modifying an image.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
