rding background elements. I\'ve re-examined the screenshots and messages, realizing the white background on Stage B is a key point. It seems they want the Stage B image to be full-screen, without the white background, like Stage A, before the usual layout. I\'m focusing on preserving the horizon line with text, which must not overlap.\n\n\n**Recalling Visual Reference**\n\nI\'m now pausing to re-examine the Odyss\303\251e Clinic website, using the provided screenshots as a crucial reference point. This reminds me that I need to establish a full-width image as the first hero section, then a two-column layout. The user wants the macro skin photograph to be the main visual, full-screen. This is a very different page construction than the current layout.\n\n\n"
