  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Font Preferences**\n\nI\'m currently focusing on the user\'s explicit dislike of the \"nova\" font. My immediate next step is to conduct a visual comparison, juxtaposing the `ODYSSE\303\211` typeface from the original reference images with the current representation of `N O V A`. This side-by-side analysis will help me understand the specific aesthetic elements the user is reacting to.\n\n\n**Identifying Font Discrepancies**\n\nI\'ve been examining the visual attributes of `ODYSSE\303\211` from the reference image, contrasting it with our app\'s `NOVA`. It\'s clear that the current implementation, using `Cormorant Garamond` with wide tracking, lacks the high-contrast, sculptural quality of a luxury editorial font. I\'m noting the importance of strong vertical stems, fine hairlines, and tighter tracking to capture the desired aesthetic, specifically comparing it to Didone/modern serif fonts like Bodoni Moda, Italiana, Cinzel, and Prata.\n\n\n**Evaluating Font Replacements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on replacing the current font with a more suitable option. My thought is to integrate **Bodoni Moda**, or alternatively **Cinzel** or **Prata**, directly into the project through Google Fonts and apply a dedicated `.font-brand` class. I will integrate the font, using the suggested cascade, across key UI elements.\n\nI\'m presently comparing `Bodoni Moda`, `Cinzel`, and `Prata`, to assess which best fits the desired appearance. In the case of `Cinzel`, I am evaluating the Roman imperial-style geometric proportions; for `Bodoni Moda`, I\'m evaluating the Parisian Didone contrast.\n\n\n**Refining Font Selection**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the specifics of `ODYSSE\303\211` to refine my font choices. I\'ve noted the flat, bracketed serifs, the high contrast between vertical and horizontal strokes, tighter spacing, and a medium-regular weight. I\'ve reevaluated `Bodoni Moda`, `Prata`, and `Playfair Display SC`, as well as including `Cinzel`, because they appear to match the Parisian luxury aesthetic. I am leaning toward integrating both `Bodoni Moda` and `Cinzel`, and applying a cascade of fonts for the `.font-brand-wordmark` class. Also, re-evaluating why `Cormorant Garamond` was failing. The uneven capital `N` and `V`, tilted `O`, and low crossbar of `A` are key indicators of why it failed.\n\n\n"
