    thinking: "**Analyzing Font Hierarchy**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the user\'s font requests. It seems we\'re defining a hierarchy: \"Medical aesthetics for timeless results\" using PS Times, and all others use Basel Grotesk. I\'m focusing on how these choices suggest emphasis and structure in the text\'s display.\n\n\n**Investigating Font Usage**\n\nI\'ve observed the user is drawing inspiration from Odyss\303\251e\'s website. They\'re keen on replicating the font hierarchy. Specifically, \"Medical aesthetics for timeless results\" is using a serif font\342\200\224likely Newsreader\342\200\224like Odyss\303\251e\'s PS Times, while other elements employ Basel Grotesk. I\'m now working to define these fonts in `src/index.css`, considering font stacks for seamless implementation.\n\n\n**Defining Font Implementation**\n\nI\'m now concretizing the CSS implementation. I\'m aiming for precise matches to the referenced website. For \"psTimes,\" I\'ll use `@font-face` aliases, ensuring Newsreader is the primary fallback for the exact proportions. Basel Grotesk will be backed by Inter or Helvetica Neue, and I\'ll load Inter and Newsreader in `index.html`. Finally, I\'m confirming the tagline font, it\'s definitely Times as per the font inspector.\n\n\n**Examining Odyss\303\251e\'s Structure**\n\nI\'m now delving into the user\'s specific concerns regarding font application. I see they\'re verifying the Odyss\303\251e website structure and font usage. They\'ve used an inspector to identify font selections, such as Basel Grotesk for several elements and Times/Newsreader for a key tagline. The goal is to accurately recreate this hierarchy in our implementation. I\'ll focus on how the tagline is displayed in the horizon bar and footer, for accurate reproduction.\n\n\n**Refining Font Metrics**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the precise typographical details. I\'ve analyzed the letter-spacing and size of several elements like \"TREATMENTS\" and \"BOOK CONSULTATION\" in the reference image. They are indeed Basel Grotesk, 11-12px, uppercase, but with tight tracking, contrary to a wider tracking value. This refinement extends to the tagline\'s size and tracking, confirming a crisp Times-like serif at 17-19px with tight spacing. I will update `index.html` and `src/index.css` to refine these details.\n\n\n"
