  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "<summary>\n## 1. Task Overview\n- **Current User Request**: Replace the portrait image in the Sanctuary Introduction section (`#introduction`, immediately below the full-screen macro skin stage) \342\200\224 which previously displayed `/images/intro-profile.jpg` (a woman washing her face) \342\200\224 with the newly uploaded portrait `/assets/aistudio/Cinematic_Profile_Portrait_of_a_Tousled-Haired_Man_097612d6.png` (saved in workspace at `/public/assets/aistudio/Cinematic_Profile_Portrait_of_a_Tousled-Haired_Man_097612d6.png`).\n- **Cumulative Session Deliverables**:\n  1. Rebrand the salon and founder from **Hershita** to **Nova** (`NOVA` wordmark, founder profile, copy, metadata, and 3D rolling marble engraving) and remove the `Reel 01 \342\200\224 Opening Ritual Film (Replay)` button from the opening hero.\n  2. Remove the overlapping *\"Beauty, in its own time.\"* headline, subheadline, and CTA buttons from Stage B of the opening hero, and replace Stage B\'s image with the full-screen (`100vh`) macro skin photograph `/assets/aistudio/Generated_Image_November_17__2026_-_4_59PM_6977a387.jpg` with no white background or top sticky header appearing until after Stage B.\n  3. Style the `NOVA` wordmark using **Cabin Sketch**, remove the bottom border line (`border-b`) under the opening horizon bar, and style the horizon bar tagline (*\"Medical aesthetics for timeless results.\"*) in **psTimes** and navigation items (`TREATMENTS`, `CONCERNS`, `ABOUT`, `BOOK CONSULTATION`) in **Basel Grotesk**.\n  4. Replace the `#introduction` left-column portrait (`/images/intro-profile.jpg`) with `/assets/aistudio/Cinematic_Profile_Portrait_of_a_Tousled-Haired_Man_097612d6.png`.\n\n## 2. Progress\n- **Completed & Verified Earlier in Session**:\n  - Updated `/index.html`, `/src/index.css`, `/src/data/salonData.ts`, `/src/App.tsx`, `/src/components/Header.tsx`, `/src/components/AboutSection.tsx`, `/src/components/InteractiveChapters.tsx`, `/src/components/TreatmentsSection.tsx`, `/src/components/RollingMarble.tsx`, and `/src/utils/bookingLogic.test.ts` for all Nova rebranding, full-screen Stage B macro skin photograph, Cabin Sketch / psTimes / Basel Grotesk typography, and borderless horizon bar.\n- **Completed Code Edit (Awaiting Final Build/Test/Browser Verification)**:\n  - Edited `/src/data/salonData.ts` (lines 81\342\200\22387) to set `SALON_CONFIG.mediaSlots.introduction.posterPath` to `\'/assets/aistudio/Cinematic_Profile_Portrait_of_a_Tousled-Haired_Man_097612d6.png\'` with `alt: \'Cinematic profile portrait of a tousled-haired man with natural skin texture\'` and `focalPoint: \'center center\'`.\n- **Skills Read**:\n  - `/skills/system_skills/ultra_mode/SKILL.md`\n  - `/skills/system_skills/computer_use/SKILL.md`\n\n## 3. Key Findings\n- In `/src/App.tsx` (lines 240\342\200\223254), the Sanctuary Introduction section (`#introduction`) renders `<MediaSlot media={mediaSlots.introduction} ... />` inside a `2/3` aspect-ratio frame on the left column (`md:col-span-3 lg:col-span-2`), matching the Odyss\303\251e reference (`media_1792862435168_88c35dd7.png`).\n- Updating `SALON_CONFIG.mediaSlots.introduction.posterPath` in `/src/data/salonData.ts` directly updates that image slot.\n\n## 4. Errors & Fixes\n- **Playwright CLI `--viewport` flag error**: Earlier in the session, `playwright-cli open ... --viewport=1440x900` failed with `Unknown option: --viewport`. Fixed by using `playwright-cli open --browser=chromium <url>` followed by `playwright-cli resize 1440 900`.\n- **Two-Column Split in Stage B Rejected by User**: When the user uploaded the macro skin photograph in Turn 3, they accidentally pasted prompt text describing a two-column split with a white/ivory right column. In Turn 4 (`no not this i want to be like full screen on the like not thing don\'t want that white bg until here`), the user clarified they wanted Stage B to remain a full-screen (`h-screen`) edge-to-edge macro skin image with no white background until `#introduction`. Fixed by deleting `src/components/ArtOfSkincareSection.tsx`, restoring full-screen Stage B in `/src/App.tsx`, and setting `Header.tsx` scroll threshold to `window.innerHeight * 1.88`.\n\n## 5. Active Context\n- Dev server is running on port 3000 (`DISABLE_HMR=true`, so `restart_dev_server` is required after edits before browser verification).\n- All Playwright browser sessions are closed (`Browser \'default\' closed`).\n\n## 6. Next Steps\n1. **Run Unit Tests, Compile, Lint, and Restart Dev Server**:\n   - Run `npx --yes tsx --test src/utils/bookingLogic.test.ts` via `run_command`.\n   - Co-execute `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` in the same response, followed by `restart_dev_server` (`waitForPreviousTools: true`).\n2. **Browser Verification (`playwright-cli`)**:\n   - Open `http://localhost:3000/?autostart=1` at `1440x900`, scroll to `#introduction` (`window.scrollTo(0, 1400)`), and capture a screenshot (`.playwright-cli/r10-intro-portrait.png`) confirming `/assets/aistudio/Cinematic_Profile_Portrait_of_a_Tousled-Haired_Man_097612d6.png` renders cleanly in the left column of the Sanctuary Introduction section, with `trap \'playwright-cli close\' EXIT`.\n3. **Final Response**:\n   - Present a concise summary to the user confirming the portrait replacement.\n\n## 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- Follow `ultra-mode` and `computer-use` rules: always co-execute `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` on the final build check, restart the dev server after code edits, and always close `playwright-cli` via `trap \'playwright-cli close\' EXIT`.\n</summary>"
    included_step_index_start: 5
    included_step_index_end: 171
    render_latest_checkpoint: true
