  user_input {
    user_response: "i want to create the scroll-driven storytelling and section transtion.\n\nMy current implementation looks like two independent stacked sections. I want a coordinated, cinematic scroll experience instead.\n\nUse GSAP and ScrollTrigger.\n\nREQUIREMENTS:\n\nCreate a pinned scroll-story section with four visual panels arranged horizontally.\n\nAs the user scrolls, keep the section pinned and progressively transition between four slides.\n\nOnly the active slide should be fully visible and prominent. Inactive slides should have reduced opacity and subtle visual fading.\n\nAnimate the active image, heading and description smoothly. Use sophisticated opacity, scale and clipping transitions.\n\nAdd a thin horizontal progress line and a dynamic slide counter, such as 01 / 04, 02 / 04, etc.\n\nConnect the final slide to the next CONCERNS / TREATMENTS section through a seamless scroll-driven transition. The next section should gradually emerge rather than simply appearing as an unrelated block after a hard section boundary.\n\nUse GSAP ScrollTrigger with pinning and scrub-based timelines. The animation progress must correspond to the user\'s actual scroll position.\n\nUse carefully timed overlapping transitions. Avoid abrupt jumps, white flashes, sudden visibility changes or excessive motion.\n\nOnce the story is complete, smoothly release the pinned section and allow normal page scrolling to continue.\n\nMake the experience responsive. On mobile, use a simplified layout with accessible navigation and avoid unnecessarily long pinning.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nFirst inspect my existing component structure and animations.\n\nModify the existing sections instead of creating duplicate sections.\n\nPreserve my typography, images, colour palette and visual design.\n\nDo not make the whole website scroll horizontally.\n\nDo not use separate scroll event listeners when GSAP ScrollTrigger can handle the timeline.\n\nClean up all ScrollTrigger instances and animations correctly in React effects.\n\nThe final result should reproduce the feeling of Odyss\303\251e\'s coordinated, scroll-driven visual storytelling, not just a normal image carousel or two stacked sections."
    items {
      text: "i want to create the scroll-driven storytelling and section transtion.\n\nMy current implementation looks like two independent stacked sections. I want a coordinated, cinematic scroll experience instead.\n\nUse GSAP and ScrollTrigger.\n\nREQUIREMENTS:\n\nCreate a pinned scroll-story section with four visual panels arranged horizontally.\n\nAs the user scrolls, keep the section pinned and progressively transition between four slides.\n\nOnly the active slide should be fully visible and prominent. Inactive slides should have reduced opacity and subtle visual fading.\n\nAnimate the active image, heading and description smoothly. Use sophisticated opacity, scale and clipping transitions.\n\nAdd a thin horizontal progress line and a dynamic slide counter, such as 01 / 04, 02 / 04, etc.\n\nConnect the final slide to the next CONCERNS / TREATMENTS section through a seamless scroll-driven transition. The next section should gradually emerge rather than simply appearing as an unrelated block after a hard section boundary.\n\nUse GSAP ScrollTrigger with pinning and scrub-based timelines. The animation progress must correspond to the user\'s actual scroll position.\n\nUse carefully timed overlapping transitions. Avoid abrupt jumps, white flashes, sudden visibility changes or excessive motion.\n\nOnce the story is complete, smoothly release the pinned section and allow normal page scrolling to continue.\n\nMake the experience responsive. On mobile, use a simplified layout with accessible navigation and avoid unnecessarily long pinning.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nFirst inspect my existing component structure and animations.\n\nModify the existing sections instead of creating duplicate sections.\n\nPreserve my typography, images, colour palette and visual design.\n\nDo not make the whole website scroll horizontally.\n\nDo not use separate scroll event listeners when GSAP ScrollTrigger can handle the timeline.\n\nClean up all ScrollTrigger instances and animations correctly in React effects.\n\nThe final result should reproduce the feeling of Odyss\303\251e\'s coordinated, scroll-driven visual storytelling, not just a normal image carousel or two stacked sections."
    }
  }
}
