  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Inspecting Requirements Meticulously**\n\nI\'m now carefully inspecting the user\'s specific requirements, cross-referencing them against our established component structure. I\'m focusing on ensuring a perfect fit between the needs expressed and the capabilities of our existing tools, particularly focusing on how to align the frontend design, ultra-mode, and computer-use skillsets to achieve this goal.\n\n\n**Analyzing Component Structure**\n\nI\'m now analyzing the existing component structure within `/src/App.tsx` and `/src/components/InteractiveChapters.tsx`. I noticed that `InteractiveChapters` is a discrete, switchable section in `App.tsx` and it renders independently of other sections. Additionally, I plan to assess the use of `gsap`, starting with a check of the `package.json` to see if it\'s currently listed as a dependency. If not, I\'ll use `install_applet_package` to install it.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Transitions**\n\nI\'m now refining the visual transition logic using GSAP and ScrollTrigger. The goal is to create a seamless pinned scroll-story with four horizontally arranged panels, ensuring active and inactive slide states. I\'m focusing on the scrub-based timeline for coordinated transitions between the \"Why Nova?\" section and the \"CONCERNS / TREATMENTS\" portal. I\'m also ensuring the design is responsive using `gsap.matchMedia()`.\n\n\n**Defining Active Slide Visuals**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on defining the visual state of the active slide. Specifically, I\'m focusing on how media veils, image wrappers, and heading/description blocks respond to active vs. inactive states, including animation details of each. I am giving special consideration to the opacity, scale, clipPath, and transform properties of the component.\n\n\n**Integrating Section Transitions**\n\nI\'m now integrating the \"CONCERNS / TREATMENTS\" portal directly into the `InteractiveChapters` scroll-story. This entails removing the standalone section and ensuring the transition from Slide 4 into the portal works seamlessly on the GSAP timeline. I\'m carefully considering how to handle the timeline phases and ensure a coordinated, scrub-based transition within the scroll-story stage, eliminating any duplication in `/src/App.tsx`.\n\n\n**Orchestrating Transition Logic**\n\nI\'m currently orchestrating the transition logic between the \"Why Nova?\" section and the \"CONCERNS / TREATMENTS\" portal. I\'m focusing on the visual cues: the \"Why Nova?\" chapter stage receding, and the portal stage smoothly emerging from below. This includes fine-tuning the `yPercent`, `scale`, and `opacity` values for a seamless visual transition on desktop. I\'m also addressing mobile responsiveness, using `gsap.matchMedia()` to ensure a different, more accessible interactive experience on smaller screens.\n\n\n"
