  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Tracing Font Instances**\n\nI\'m focused on tracking down every instance of \"Nova\" and \"NOVA\" in the UI. My goal is to standardize the font usage as per the user\'s specific request, ensuring consistency across all applications of the font family. I am meticulously reviewing each element.\n\n\n**Analyzing Font Renderings**\n\nI\'ve made great strides in identifying instances of \"Nova\" and \"NOVA\" within the UI. I have confirmed that everywhere we use the string, it\'s rendered as the `font-brand`, which is Cabin Sketch, uppercase. I\'ve compiled a list: the Opening Hero Horizon Bar, Primary Sticky Header, and Menu Overlay all utilize the `font-brand` instance. I\'ve also found an explicit instance of `NOVA` with a tracking class. The Sanctuary Introduction Headline uses the `font-brand` styled uppercase `NOVA` inside a larger text string.\n\n\n**Examining Font Implementations**\n\nI\'ve progressed further, examining how \"NOVA\" is integrated in `InteractiveChapters` and `App.tsx`. In `InteractiveChapters`, it\'s rendered with specific tracking, while in `App.tsx`\'s \"Our Philosophy\" section, I\'ve noted a distinct layout with different font styling for \"OUR PHILOSOPHY\" and \"NOVA\" in the left and right columns. I\'m taking note of all styles involved.\n\n\n**Pinpointing Font Applications**\n\nI\'m now identifying additional usages of the target fonts. I\'ve located a five-line block of editorial serif text with specific styling, and the \"EXPLORE TREATMENTS\" label below it. I\'ve also found two instances of \"`NOVA`\" within the \"Explore More / Our Approach\" section and the `TreatmentsSection`, both using the `font-brand` styling with tracking.\n\n\n**Locating Font Usage**\n\nI\'ve located further instances of \"NOVA\" in the `AboutSection`, specifically in the consultation link, the founder\'s description, and within a conditional render. Additionally, the footer references the brand name, rendered in the `font-brand` style. Regarding the serif font, I\'ve confirmed it\'s utilized with unique styling: light weight, high-contrast, and specific tracking.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
