  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Layout Behavior**\n\nI\'ve been examining the layout implementation, specifically `App.tsx`. It appears the absence of `overflow-hidden` on relevant elements like `#top` and the content containers allows the intended sticky behavior of the right-hand video and header to function correctly. This is good news, as the use of `lg:sticky lg:top-24` can proceed as planned, and we can adjust the video aspect ratio accordingly.\n\n\n**Refining Sticky Positioning**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how CSS Grid and sticky positioning interact. The grid item containing the left-hand video and caption stretches to match the taller right-hand video\'s height. Inside that grid item, the sticky wrapper will ensure the video and caption stay fixed at the top, scrolling alongside the larger video. I\'m making sure `items-stretch` doesn\'t affect the scroll glide.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
