  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Visual Constraints**\n\nI\'m now investigating how to visually adjust the larger video to create a vertical emphasis, and also, how to implement a scrolling effect for the smaller video that continues until its end. I\'m focusing on the visual needs and the technical implementation of each.\n\n\n**Implementing Full Scrolling**\n\nI\'m now focusing on ensuring the small video\'s caption scrolls completely to the bottom of the larger video. I\'m reviewing `/src/App.tsx` and evaluating the existing layout, specifically lines 316-360, to assess how to achieve this visual effect within the existing column structure, with the aspect ratios of the videos. I\'m determining how to ensure the scrolling feels appropriate, depending on the screen height.\n\n\n**Evaluating Vertical Design**\n\nI\'m now investigating how to define a truly vertical editorial structure. I\'m considering aspect ratios like `[3/4.6]` and `min-h-[1280px]` for various screen sizes, as well as exploring column spans. I am also pondering the user\'s intent with \"scrolling until the end\" and its implications. I\'m now examining `position: sticky` and GSAP ScrollTrigger, and how `philosophy-small-sticky-card` behaves at the end of scrolling.\n\n\n**Investigating Caption Behavior**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the caption\'s behavior in relation to the smaller video and larger video. I\'m checking if the small card can smoothly travel down to the bottom of the bigger video, and if not, how to achieve that effect. I\'m also reviewing `lg:sticky` to see why it might not be scrolling all the way. I\'ll test it using Playwright or calculate the geometry. Also, I\'m trying to see why `midSmallTop` and `midLargeTop` were both equal. I\'m looking back at Playwright output.\n\n\n**Revisiting Scroll Behavior**\n\nOkay, I\'ve got a critical realization: the `window.scrollBy(0, 520)` call isn\'t immediately reflecting in the measurements due to the smooth scrolling behavior defined in `/src/index.css`. The page\'s scroll animation happens asynchronously, so those measurements are incorrect. The `lg:sticky` class isn\'t doing anything while the smooth scrolling is active. This changes my approach entirely. I need to rethink how I\'m measuring and triggering events, since `lg:sticky` does stick at the end.\n\n\n"
