  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Scroll Behavior**\n\nOkay, I\'m diving into the Playwright run data. Specifically, I\'m puzzled by the `startOffset` value of `1103`. Why isn\'t it closer to zero, especially after initially scrolling down to the bottom and then back up using `window.scrollTo`? I\'m now examining the `App.tsx` file and the associated scroll logic to understand this discrepancy.\n\n\n**Investigating Sticky Position**\n\nI\'ve realized a major flaw: GSAP\'s `ScrollTrigger` might be the problem, as it relies on absolute scroll coordinates that shift when elements above pin. I\'m now looking at native CSS `position: sticky` within the grid column, which should be immune to these shifts. Earlier tests might have failed because of how Playwright was interacting with it. I\'m investigating why `position: sticky` didn\'t work previously, specifically in conjunction with the `window.scrollTo` calls.\n\n\n"
