    thinking: "**Analyzing Visual Data**\n\nI\'m focusing intently on the image and the user\'s instructions. Currently, I\'m parsing the request to understand the intended alterations to the cursor and the \"sphere ball.\" I\'m identifying the specific area and trying to determine the meaning behind \"Hershita\". I am attempting to ensure this is understood and captured.\n\n\n**Interpreting User Intent**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the cursor\'s behavior in the image. The user wants the cursor to transform within the studio cyclorama. I\'m considering the meaning of \"Hershita\" in relation to the cursor follower and also considering the potential engraving on the sphere. I need to clarify if \"Hershita\" applies to both or just one of these elements.\n\n\n**Revising Sphere Details**\n\nI\'ve made significant adjustments to my mental model of the sphere. The engraving is vertical, in a refined serif font (ODYSS\303\211E), not horizontal like my current code. I\'m focusing on the visual discrepancies between the reference image and my previous assumptions, particularly the absence of static text in the studio cyclorama and the sphere\'s centered position.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Specifications**\n\nI am now focusing on the sphere\'s visual details. I\'ve refined my mental image to incorporate the soft studio shadow angle and the champagne-pearl metallic sheen. The vertical engraved typography and dark-bronze carved deboss are also clarified. I\'m taking the 90-degree rotation of the text into account, to ensure it matches the reference image.\n\n\n**Clarifying Text Assignment**\n\nI\'m now certain about \"Hershita.\" The user wants the custom cursor, when hovering over the specified area, to display \"\342\227\217 Hershita\". My focus is on the sphere\'s photorealism now, like in the screenshot. The goal is to make the sphere visual better and like in the reference image.\n\n\n**Visualizing Sphere Details**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the visual properties of the pearl sphere. My focus is on the studio lighting and the cyclorama\'s clean backdrop. I\'m exploring the nuances of the satin pearl-champagne metallic sheen and the subtle left-directional shadow. I\'m also confirming the vertical engraving of \"NOVA\" based on the \"ODYSS\303\211E\" example, ensuring the top-to-bottom vertical text follows the curvature.\n\n\n**Defining Cursor Functionality**\n\nI\'m now integrating the interactive cursor behavior. The entire cyclorama will be clickable with a \"cursor-none\" on hover for desktops. A floating badge will follow the mouse inside the container. It\'s a solid white circle with \"Hershita\" in white sans-serif. When the mouse isn\'t active, the badge returns to its resting position.\n\n\n**Calculating Sphere Position**\n\nI am now carefully analyzing the sphere\'s dimensions and placement within the cyclorama. I\'ve calculated the radius based on screen size (approximately 82-92px radius), and determined its center position near the image\'s center, slightly left. I am focused on refining my understanding of the shadow to determine its impact.\n\n\n\n**Analyzing Sphere\'s Shading**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the sphere\'s material properties. It\'s a satin pearl-champagne metallic sheen, not a flat color. I\'m focusing on the distinct shading: warm bronze-taupe shadow on top, muted taupe-silver on the left, and a luminous pearl specular sheen on the right. I\'m also ensuring the floor bounce is reflected on the bottom right.\n\n\n\n**Modeling Sphere Typography**\n\nI\'m now focused on the sphere\'s engraved text. I\'m using true 3D spherical latitude and longitude coordinates to place and render each letter realistically. The letters are carved with dark bronze interiors, warm-white bevel highlights, and subtle shadows. I am also planning to roll the sphere so that the meridian band shifts slightly in longitude.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_6918422530270312389"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"import React, { useEffect, useRef, useState } from \'react\';\\n\\ninterface RollingMarbleProps {\\n  brandText?: string;\\n  onBookClick: () => void;\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Photorealistic studio-lit satin pearl-champagne sphere with vertical 3D meridian\\n * engraving and custom \\\"\342\227\217 Hershita\\\" cursor follower across the cyclorama area,\\n * matching reference `image_9f727fd1.png`.\\n */\\nexport const RollingMarble: React.FC<RollingMarbleProps> = ({\\n  brandText = \'NOVA\',\\n  onBookClick,\\n}) => {\\n  const containerRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement | null>(null);\\n  const canvasRef = useRef<HTMLCanvasElement | null>(null);\\n  const cursorDotRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement | null>(null);\\n  const scrollBoostRef = useRef<number>(0);\\n\\n  // Track whether the user\'s pointer is inside the cyclorama area\\n  const [isPointerInside, setIsPointerInside] = useState(false);\\n  const pointerTargetRef = useRef<{ x: number; y: number } | null>(null);\\n  const pointerCurrentRef = useRef<{ x: number; y: number }>({ x: 0, y: 0 });\\n  const mouseNormXRef = useRef<number>(0);\\n\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    let lastScrollY = window.scrollY;\\n    const handleScroll = () => {\\n      const dy = window.scrollY - lastScrollY;\\n      lastScrollY = window.scrollY;\\n      scrollBoostRef.current = Math.max(-0.07, Math.min(0.07, dy * 0.0018));\\n    };\\n    window.addEventListener(\'scroll\', handleScroll, { passive: true });\\n    return () => window.removeEventListener(\'scroll\', handleScroll);\\n  }, []);\\n\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const canvas = canvasRef.current;\\n    const container = containerRef.current;\\n    if (!canvas || !container) return;\\n    const ctx = canvas.getContext(\'2d\');\\n    if (!ctx) return;\\n\\n    // Offscreen high-DPI vertical meridian strip texture\\n    // Height maps to latitude (-PI/2 at top pole to +PI/2 at bottom pole)\\n    const stripW = 260;\\n    const stripH = 1200;\\n    const stripCanvas = document.createElement(\'canvas\');\\n    stripCanvas.width = stripW;\\n    stripCanvas.height = stripH;\\n    const sctx = stripCanvas.getContext(\'2d\');\\n\\n    const drawVerticalEngravingStrip = () => {\\n      if (!sctx) return;\\n      sctx.clearRect(0, 0, stripW, stripH);\\n\\n      sctx.save();\\n      // Translate to center of strip and rotate 90deg clockwise so text runs vertically top-to-bottom\\n      sctx.translate(stripW * 0.5, stripH * 0.5);\\n      sctx.rotate(Math.PI / 2);\\n\\n      const word = brandText.toUpperCase();\\n      // Stretch vertically slightly to match the tall, architectural engraved serif in image_9f727fd1.png\\n      sctx.scale(1.08, 1.32);\\n      sctx.font = \'300 132px \\\"psTimes\\\", \\\"Newsreader\\\", \\\"Times New Roman\\\", serif\';\\n      sctx.textAlign = \'center\';\\n      sctx.textBaseline = \'middle\';\\n\\n      // Spread letters slightly so they span from upper pole to lower pole\\n      const trackedWord = word.split(\'\').join(\'\\\\u200A\');\\n\\n      // 1. Bright specular catchlight on the lower-right carved bevel (key light from right)\\n      sctx.fillStyle = \'rgba(255, 253, 248, 0.78)\';\\n      sctx.fillText(trackedWord, 1.8, -1.8);\\n\\n      // 2. Soft warm inner bevel shadow\\n      sctx.fillStyle = \'rgba(72, 62, 50, 0.55)\';\\n      sctx.fillText(trackedWord, -1.6, 1.6);\\n\\n      // 3. Deep carved bronze-obsidian core engraving\\n      sctx.fillStyle = \'#241F1A\';\\n      sctx.fillText(trackedWord, 0, 0);\\n\\n      sctx.restore();\\n    };\\n\\n    drawVerticalEngravingStrip();\\n    if (document.fonts && document.fonts.ready) {\\n      document.fonts.ready.then(() => {\\n        drawVerticalEngravingStrip();\\n      });\\n    }\\n\\n    let animationFrameId = 0;\\n    let timePhase = 0;\\n\\n    const renderFrame = () => {\\n      const dpr = Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio || 1, 2);\\n      const rect = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();\\n      const width = Math.max(320, rect.width);\\n      const height = Math.max(320, rect.height);\\n\\n      if (\\n        canvas.width !== Math.floor(width * dpr) ||\\n        canvas.height !== Math.floor(height * dpr)\\n      ) {\\n        canvas.width = Math.floor(width * dpr);\\n        canvas.height = Math.floor(height * dpr);\\n      }\\n\\n      // Smoothly update custom cursor position (either following mouse or resting to the right of the sphere)\\n      const R = Math.min(width, height) * 0.195;\\n      const rollOsc = Math.sin(timePhase * 0.75) * 0.35 + mouseNormXRef.current * 0.35;\\n      const cx = width * 0.49 + rollOsc * (width * 0.018);\\n      const cy = height * 0.53;\\n\\n      const defaultCursorX = cx + R + 34;\\n      const defaultCursorY = cy + R * 0.14;\\n      const targetX = pointerTargetRef.current ? pointerTargetRef.current.x : defaultCursorX;\\n      const targetY = pointerTargetRef.current ? pointerTargetRef.current.y : defaultCursorY;\\n\\n      if (pointerCurrentRef.current.x === 0 && pointerCurrentRef.current.y === 0) {\\n        pointerCurrentRef.current = { x: targetX, y: targetY };\\n      } else {\\n        pointerCurrentRef.current.x += (targetX - pointerCurrentRef.current.x) * 0.18;\\n        pointerCurrentRef.current.y += (targetY - pointerCurrentRef.current.y) * 0.18;\\n      }\\n\\n      if (cursorDotRef.current) {\\n        cursorDotRef.current.style.transform = `translate3d(${pointerCurrentRef.current.x}px, ${pointerCurrentRef.current.y}px, 0)`;\\n      }\\n\\n      ctx.save();\\n      ctx.scale(dpr, dpr);\\n\\n      // 1. Seamless Studio Cyclorama Backdrop (#CECECE top -> #D4D4D4 mid -> #DADADA floor)\\n      const bgGrad = ctx.createLinearGradient(0, 0, 0, height);\\n      bgGrad.addColorStop(0, \'#CCCCCC\');\\n      bgGrad.addColorStop(0.48, \'#D2D2D2\');\\n      bgGrad.addColorStop(0.75, \'#D7D7D7\');\\n      bgGrad.addColorStop(1, \'#DCDCDC\');\\n      ctx.fillStyle = bgGrad;\\n      ctx.fillRect(0, 0, width, height);\\n\\n      // Soft studio key-light glow on the right side of the cyclorama floor\\n      const studioGlow = ctx.createRadialGradient(\\n        cx + R * 0.9,\\n        cy + R * 0.2,\\n        R * 0.2,\\n        cx + R * 0.4,\\n        cy + R * 0.2,\\n        width * 0.48\\n      );\\n      studioGlow.addColorStop(0, \'rgba(248, 247, 244, 0.42)\');\\n      studioGlow.addColorStop(0.55, \'rgba(225, 225, 223, 0.14)\');\\n      studioGlow.addColorStop(1, \'rgba(210, 210, 210, 0)\');\\n      ctx.fillStyle = studioGlow;\\n      ctx.fillRect(0, 0, width, height);\\n\\n      // 2. Long Soft Studio Cast Shadow Extending Left & Slightly Upward (matching `image_9f727fd1.png`)\\n      ctx.save();\\n      ctx.translate(cx - R * 1.45, cy + R * 0.36);\\n      ctx.rotate(0.16);\\n      ctx.scale(2.65, 0.46);\\n      const castShadowGrad = ctx.createRadialGradient(\\n        R * 0.55,\\n        0,\\n        R * 0.08,\\n        0,\\n        0,\\n        R * 1.65\\n      );\\n      castShadowGrad.addColorStop(0, \'rgba(118, 113, 105, 0.44)\');\\n      castShadowGrad.addColorStop(0.38, \'rgba(142, 138, 131, 0.26)\');\\n      castShadowGrad.addColorStop(0.72, \'rgba(175, 172, 168, 0.11)\');\\n      castShadowGrad.addColorStop(1, \'rgba(208, 208, 208, 0)\');\\n      ctx.fillStyle = castShadowGrad;\\n      ctx.beginPath();\\n      ctx.arc(0, 0, R * 1.65, 0, Math.PI * 2);\\n      ctx.fill();\\n      ctx.restore();\\n\\n      // Secondary tighter penumbra shadow near the left base of the sphere\\n      ctx.save();\\n      ctx.translate(cx - R * 0.62, cy + R * 0.72);\\n      ctx.rotate(0.08);\\n      ctx.scale(1.55, 0.3);\\n      const midShadowGrad = ctx.createRadialGradient(\\n        R * 0.25,\\n        0,\\n        R * 0.04,\\n        0,\\n        0,\\n        R * 1.05\\n      );\\n      midShadowGrad.addColorStop(0, \'rgba(84, 78, 70, 0.48)\');\\n      midShadowGrad.addColorStop(0.55, \'rgba(124, 118, 110, 0.22)\');\\n      midShadowGrad.addColorStop(1, \'rgba(190, 188, 184, 0)\');\\n      ctx.fillStyle = midShadowGrad;\\n      ctx.beginPath();\\n      ctx.arc(0, 0, R * 1.05, 0, Math.PI * 2);\\n      ctx.fill();\\n      ctx.restore();\\n\\n      // 3. Crisp Contact Occlusion Shadow Directly Under the Sphere\'s Base\\n      ctx.save();\\n      ctx.translate(cx - R * 0.08, cy + R * 0.96);\\n      ctx.scale(0.95, 0.16);\\n      const aoGrad = ctx.createRadialGradient(0, 0, R * 0.04, 0, 0, R * 0.85);\\n      aoGrad.addColorStop(0, \'rgba(38, 33, 28, 0.68)\');\\n      aoGrad.addColorStop(0.5, \'rgba(78, 72, 64, 0.32)\');\\n      aoGrad.addColorStop(1, \'rgba(160, 156, 150, 0)\');\\n      ctx.fillStyle = aoGrad;\\n      ctx.beginPath();\\n      ctx.arc(0, 0, R * 0.85, 0, Math.PI * 2);\\n      ctx.fill();\\n      ctx.restore();\\n\\n      // 4. Satin Pearl-Champagne Sphere Body (Clipped to Circle)\\n      ctx.save();\\n      ctx.beginPath();\\n      ctx.arc(cx, cy, R, 0, Math.PI * 2);\\n      ctx.clip();\\n\\n      // Base metallic champagne-pearl gradient:\\n      // Bright warm-white pearl on right-center face, rich bronze-taupe crown on upper-left\\n      const baseSphereGrad = ctx.createRadialGradient(\\n        cx + R * 0.34,\\n        cy + R * 0.06,\\n        R * 0.04,\\n        cx - R * 0.12,\\n        cy - R * 0.12,\\n        R * 1.24\\n      );\\n      baseSphereGrad.addColorStop(0, \'#FCFBF9\');\\n      baseSphereGrad.addColorStop(0.22, \'#F1EDE6\');\\n      baseSphereGrad.addColorStop(0.48, \'#D7D0C4\');\\n      baseSphereGrad.addColorStop(0.74, \'#AFA696\');\\n      baseSphereGrad.addColorStop(0.92, \'#8F8575\');\\n      baseSphereGrad.addColorStop(1, \'#A69D8E\');\\n      ctx.fillStyle = baseSphereGrad;\\n      ctx.fillRect(cx - R, cy - R, R * 2, R * 2);\\n\\n      // Upper-crown bronze-taupe shading (matches the warm dark metallic top of the sphere in `image_9f727fd1.png`)\\n      const crownShade = ctx.createRadialGradient(\\n        cx - R * 0.18,\\n        cy - R * 0.82,\\n        R * 0.05,\\n        cx - R * 0.1,\\n        cy - R * 0.45,\\n        R * 0.95\\n      );\\n      crownShade.addColorStop(0, \'rgba(106, 95, 78, 0.62)\');\\n      crownShade.addColorStop(0.45, \'rgba(132, 121, 104, 0.28)\');\\n      crownShade.addColorStop(1, \'rgba(165, 156, 142, 0)\');\\n      ctx.fillStyle = crownShade;\\n      ctx.fillRect(cx - R, cy - R, R * 2, R * 2);\\n\\n      // 5. True 3D Spherical Latitude Projection of the Vertical Engraved Wordmark\\n      // Slices the vertical strip horizontally by latitude (-PI/2 to +PI/2) so letters curve\\n      // and foreshorten naturally over the top crown and bottom base of the sphere!\\n      ctx.save();\\n      ctx.translate(cx, cy);\\n\\n      const rows = 96;\\n      const lonOffset = -0.06 + Math.sin(timePhase * 0.75) * 0.08 + mouseNormXRef.current * 0.1;\\n\\n      for (let i = 0; i < rows; i++) {\\n        const ny0 = (i / rows) * 2 - 1;\\n        const ny1 = ((i + 1) / rows) * 2 - 1;\\n        const nyMid = (ny0 + ny1) * 0.5;\\n\\n        // Latitude on the sphere (-PI/2 at top pole, +PI/2 at bottom pole)\\n        const lat = Math.asin(Math.max(-1, Math.min(1, nyMid)));\\n        const cosLat = Math.cos(lat);\\n        if (cosLat <= 0.06) continue;\\n\\n        // Map latitude (-PI/2 .. +PI/2) to vertical coordinate in stripCanvas\\n        const vNorm = (lat / Math.PI) + 0.5; // 0..1\\n        // Span 88% of the pole-to-pole arc so top & bottom letters curve right to the edges like ODYSS\303\211E\\n        const vMapped = (vNorm - 0.5) * 1.06 + 0.5;\\n        if (vMapped < 0.01 || vMapped > 0.99) continue;\\n\\n        const srcY = Math.floor(vMapped * (stripH - 4));\\n        const srcH = Math.max(2, Math.ceil(stripH / rows));\\n\\n        const destY = ny0 * R;\\n        const destH = Math.max(1.5, (ny1 - ny0) * R + 0.85);\\n\\n        // Horizontal 3D wrap: width compresses toward top/bottom poles and shifts with longitude\\n        const bandW = R * 0.42 * (0.55 + 0.45 * cosLat);\\n        const shiftX = Math.sin(lonOffset) * R * cosLat;\\n\\n        // Limb darkening near the very top/bottom poles\\n        ctx.globalAlpha = Math.pow(cosLat, 0.55) * 0.95;\\n\\n        ctx.drawImage(\\n          stripCanvas,\\n          0,\\n          srcY,\\n          stripW,\\n          srcH,\\n          shiftX - bandW * 0.5,\\n          destY,\\n          bandW,\\n          destH\\n        );\\n      }\\n      ctx.restore();\\n\\n      // 6. Broad Satin Specular Highlight on the Right Face (Studio Softbox Reflection)\\n      const specGrad = ctx.createRadialGradient(\\n        cx + R * 0.36,\\n        cy + R * 0.04,\\n        R * 0.02,\\n        cx + R * 0.26,\\n        cy + R * 0.04,\\n        R * 0.62\\n      );\\n      specGrad.addColorStop(0, \'rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.72)\');\\n      specGrad.addColorStop(0.42, \'rgba(255, 253, 249, 0.26)\');\\n      specGrad.addColorStop(1, \'rgba(255, 255, 255, 0)\');\\n      ctx.fillStyle = specGrad;\\n      ctx.fillRect(cx - R, cy - R, R * 2, R * 2);\\n\\n      // 7. Delicate Fresnel Rim Reflection Around the Sphere\'s Lower & Left-Right Perimeter\\n      const rimGrad = ctx.createRadialGradient(cx, cy, R * 0.82, cx, cy, R);\\n      rimGrad.addColorStop(0, \'rgba(255, 255, 255, 0)\');\\n      rimGrad.addColorStop(0.75, \'rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04)\');\\n      rimGrad.addColorStop(0.94, \'rgba(245, 242, 236, 0.28)\');\\n      rimGrad.addColorStop(1, \'rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.48)\');\\n      ctx.fillStyle = rimGrad;\\n      ctx.fillRect(cx - R, cy - R, R * 2, R * 2);\\n\\n      ctx.restore(); // end sphere clip\\n\\n      // Subtle anti-aliased outer ring to blend sphere edge into the studio cyclorama\\n      ctx.strokeStyle = \'rgba(150, 144, 134, 0.22)\';\\n      ctx.lineWidth = 1;\\n      ctx.beginPath();\\n      ctx.arc(cx, cy, R, 0, Math.PI * 2);\\n      ctx.stroke();\\n\\n      ctx.restore();\\n\\n      // Smoothly advance phase\\n      timePhase += 0.012 + scrollBoostRef.current;\\n      scrollBoostRef.current *= 0.9;\\n\\n      animationFrameId = window.requestAnimationFrame(renderFrame);\\n    };\\n\\n    renderFrame();\\n    return () => window.cancelAnimationFrame(animationFrameId);\\n  }, [brandText]);\\n\\n  const handleMouseMove = (e: React.MouseEvent<HTMLDivElement>) => {\\n    const rect = e.currentTarget.getBoundingClientRect();\\n    const x = e.clientX - rect.left;\\n    const y = e.clientY - rect.top;\\n    pointerTargetRef.current = { x, y };\\n    mouseNormXRef.current = ((x / Math.max(1, rect.width)) - 0.5) * 2;\\n    if (!isPointerInside) setIsPointerInside(true);\\n  };\\n\\n  const handleMouseLeave = () => {\\n    setIsPointerInside(false);\\n    pointerTargetRef.current = null;\\n    mouseNormXRef.current = 0;\\n  };\\n\\n  return (\\n    <div\\n      ref={containerRef}\\n      role=\\\"button\\\"\\n      tabIndex={0}\\n      aria-label=\\\"Hershita \342\200\224 Begin your tailored journey\\\"\\n      onClick={onBookClick}\\n      onKeyDown={(e) => {\\n        if (e.key === \'Enter\' || e.key === \' \') {\\n          e.preventDefault();\\n          onBookClick();\\n        }\\n      }}\\n      onMouseMove={handleMouseMove}\\n      onMouseEnter={() => setIsPointerInside(true)}\\n      onMouseLeave={handleMouseLeave}\\n      className={`relative h-[66vh] min-h-[460px] max-h-[700px] w-full overflow-hidden bg-[#D2D2D2] select-none focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-[#18224B] ${\\n        isPointerInside ? \'lg:cursor-none\' : \'cursor-pointer\'\\n      }`}\\n    >\\n      <canvas\\n        ref={canvasRef}\\n        aria-label={`Rolling pearlescent marble engraved with ${brandText}`}\\n        className=\\\"block h-full w-full\\\"\\n      />\\n\\n      {/* Custom Floating Cursor Follower (\\\"\342\227\217 Hershita\\\") matching `image_9f727fd1.png` */}\\n      <div\\n        ref={cursorDotRef}\\n        data-testid=\\\"marble-cursor-follower\\\"\\n        className=\\\"pointer-events-none absolute left-0 top-0 z-20 -translate-y-1/2 flex items-center gap-2.5 whitespace-nowrap will-change-transform\\\"\\n      >\\n        <span\\n          aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\"\\n          className=\\\"h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-white shadow-[0_0_8px_rgba(255,255,255,0.85)]\\\"\\n        />\\n        <span className=\\\"font-basel text-[13.5px] font-normal tracking-[-0.01em] text-white drop-shadow-[0_1px_6px_rgba(0,0,0,0.16)]\\\">\\n          Hershita\\n        </span>\\n      </div>\\n    </div>\\n  );\\n};\\n\",\"Description\":\"Upgrade RollingMarble.tsx with photorealistic satin pearl-champagne 3D sphere, vertical meridian engraving, and custom \'\342\227\217 Hershita\' cursor follower matching image_9f727fd1.png\",\"Overwrite\":true,\"TargetFile\":\"/src/components/RollingMarble.tsx\",\"toolAction\":\"Upgrading RollingMarble sphere and cursor follower\",\"toolSummary\":\"Upgrade RollingMarble sphere and cursor follower\"}"
