  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Logo Hover States**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of the two screenshots. I\'m focusing on the logo and meticulously studying its visual changes when the mouse hovers over it. This initial investigation will help to identify the variations of the UI as a result of mouse interactions.\n\n\n**Analyzing Typographic Animation**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the typographic animation of the logo. The connected \"SS\" in \"ODYSS\303\211E\" transforms via a horizontal flip, becoming mirrored \"\306\247\306\247.\" This concept extends to \"NOVA,\" where letters mirror or interlock. Specifically, `N`\'s diagonal stroke flips, and `V` and `A` mirror each other on hover, creating a dynamic visual effect that I am analyzing across all instances of the \"NOVA\" wordmark.\n\n\n**Developing Wordmark Component**\n\nI\'m now building the reusable `<NovaWordmark />` component. I\'m focusing on the animation logic and ensuring the horizontal mirroring effect, particularly on the letters `N` and `V`, is implemented exactly as it should be. The goal is to make it feel super crispy and dynamic, just like the `SS` flip.\n\n\n**Refining Letter Transformations**\n\nI\'m now refining the letter transformations for the \"NOVA\" wordmark on hover. The core idea is to mirror certain letters horizontally like the \"SS\" in \"ODYSS\303\211E.\" Specifically, I\'m focusing on flipping the `N` into `\320\230`. For the `V` and `A`, I am now experimenting with vertical mirroring/rotation, and a custom ligature to achieve an interlocking effect reminiscent of the `SS` transformation.\n\n\n"
